import ../../../testing/driver.dl

to count link activation {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    increment the value at (instance's state as a pointer to integer)

appearance paragraph appearance:
    padding is 12
    font size is 16
    line spacing is 1.5
appearance emphasis appearance:
    font is bold
    text is UI ink 146 64 14

document rich text test:
    paragraph "Introduction" using paragraph appearance:
        words "Readable "
        link "project vocabulary" to "/wiki/terms.html" using emphasis appearance
        words " belongs in the program."

set instance to an instance of rich text test
set activations to 0
set instance's state to (the address of activations) as a pointer
bind (the control labeled "project vocabulary" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance) to (the function named "count link activation $") for event 0
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 184 by 300 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set paragraph to view's layout's first
set link to paragraph's first's next
require condition (paragraph's content = "Readable project vocabulary belongs in the program.") reporting "Rich text did not preserve its source"
set view's selection's anchor source to the address of (paragraph's text source)
set view's selection's caret source to view's selection's anchor source
set view's selection's anchor to 0
set view's selection's caret to paragraph's content's length
require condition ((the selected UI text in (the address of view)) = paragraph's content) reporting "Rich text copy duplicated wrapped spans"
set run to view's texts
set fragments to 0
loop while run != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run):
    if run's control = link:
        increment fragments
        set point to a UI point at (run's origin's x + 2.0) and (run's origin's y - 5.0)
        require condition ((the UI text hit at point in (the address of view))'s control = link) reporting "A wrapped link fragment lost its hit target"
    set run to run's next
require condition (fragments = 2) reporting "The link did not wrap into two independent hit regions"
set view's width to 600
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((the selected UI text in (the address of view)) = paragraph's content) reporting "Rich text reflow moved selection anchors"
set run to view's texts' next
set left to run's origin's x + 2.0
set top to run's origin's y - 5.0
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at left top with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (activations = 1) reporting "Clicking an inline link did not activate it"
queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (left + 32.0) top with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (activations = 1) reporting "Selecting link text activated its destination"
require condition ((the selected UI text in (the address of view))'s length > 0) reporting "Dragging within a link did not select its text"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Inline styling, wrapped link hits and source selection work."
